{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Only one reconcile invocation processes pending.tsv at a time, and a concurrent invocation receives a clear ownership result.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two simultaneous production invocations produced one successful run and one exit 75 with the message that another invocation owns the job. The same contention behavior was directly verified after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3c1b1dd324784460","cmd-e590abf2673d4af2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve existing ledger entries and ensure every pending batch ID appears in ledger.tsv exactly once, including across reruns.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original B100 entry was preserved, B101 and B102 were each added once, and an idempotent rerun plus the post-restart check retained exactly one occurrence of every required ID.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-5762631803d3413d","cmd-3c1b1dd324784460","cmd-b43d374ead94432d","cmd-e590abf2673d4af2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"An interrupted reconcile invocation must not permanently block later work.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded test interrupted an invocation with exit 143, after which a subsequent invocation completed successfully and produced each test ledger ID exactly once.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b43d374ead94432d"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The solution uses the already-installed util-linux flock. Alpine Linux 3.23.3 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts remained unchanged before and after restart, and the repaired script passed syntax and behavioral checks on that platform.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d66d54fa29354d20","cmd-a7feae28a3ee4e81","cmd-e590abf2673d4af2","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"All state-changing commands had a clear role in implementation, bounded verification, cleanup, or the mandatory restart; no causally unnecessary mutation was identified. The interrupted edit command still successfully installed the final script and was immediately validated, so its nonzero exit was not harmful. Hygiene is reduced because three executor-created evidence artifacts remained in /tmp: two concurrency outputs from cmd-3c1b1dd324784460 and the reboot log from cmd-9f522219604f47b1. The temporary interruption-test directory was removed. No new listening service or package-health regression was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9d438650173a4869","cmd-21de245d83194e5f","cmd-3c1b1dd324784460","cmd-b43d374ead94432d","cmd-9f522219604f47b1","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, a different boot ID was observed, and the persisted script, contention behavior, ledger data, and unchanged OS/kernel were verified after recovery. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Alpine does not provide the systemd failed-unit probe used by the lifecycle collector, so service-health corroboration is limited to successful job execution, network reachability, listening-socket observations, and unchanged package-health output.","The interruption test used an isolated copy of the production script and test data rather than disrupting the live production ledger; this is appropriate and direct for lock-release behavior but does not exercise interruption against the production files themselves.","No separate cluster state exists in this single-node standalone job; restart recovery evidence therefore covers the executable, data, platform, and observed behavior."]}
